.TH NEXUS 1 "October 2026" "NEXUS 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nexus \- terminal-native Linux network control center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nexus
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NEXUS inspects interfaces, sockets, routes, DNS and bandwidth in a full-screen
terminal. Press d for diagnostics or Ctrl+K for the command palette.
External tests require explicit consent. Network configuration changes are
previewed and confirmed before execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --doctor
List available optional system tools.
.TP
.B --snapshot
Print a local network snapshot as JSON without external requests.
.TP
.BI --report " PATH"
Write a redacted local report. Use a .txt suffix for text output.
.TP
.B --include-sensitive
Include private endpoints and process information in a report.
.TP
.B --fresh
Ignore saved history and do not persist session settings or history.
.TP
.BI --theme " NAME"
Use dark, oled, catppuccin, tokyo-night, gruvbox or light.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/nexus-net/config.toml
.br
.I ~/.local/share/nexus-net/history.json
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+K commands; d diagnose; Tab next page; j/k move; Enter inspect;
/ filter; ? help; x cancel a diagnostic; q exit.
